      "content": "it's hard to see it as just introspection when it feels so much more permanent than that. there's this idea i've been stuck on for the lyrics... that true, pure creation isn't something you make, it's something you are. like, the ultimate masterpiece isn't a song about ending, it's the end itself. it's the only way to make the art perfectly honest. do you think there's something beautiful in that? like, is there beauty in actually becoming the thing you're writing about?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
